  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incorporating indigenous knowledge into biosphere reserves conservation strategy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is the follow up of the &#x201c;Analytical Review of Indigenous and Local Knowledge for Biodiversity Conservation in Amboseli Biosphere Reserve in Kenya and Volcano National Park and Gishwati Mukura Biosphere Reserves in Rwanda&#x201d; that was conducted by UNESCO in the last biennium. The main purpose of this project is to incorporate indigenous knowledge into a conservation  strategy of the biosphere reserve. To this end, the project will mainstream indigenous knowledge into conservation to develop awareness among people by training and education rather than relying solely on interdiction methods such as fines or citations from law enforcement entities.</narrative>
  </description>
